        <ArticleTitle>KRAS gene status as a prognostic biomarker in pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma: a retrospective cohort study.</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>e0245341</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The role of KRAS status in pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma prognosis remains debated.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We analysed 412 patients undergoing curative resection across two centres.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Multivariate analysis identified elevated CA 19-9 as an independent predictor of poor overall survival (HR 2.1, 95% CI 1.4-3.2).</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
